<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Okayama Prefecture</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1871</span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/okayama">Okayama</a> Prefecture is a prefecture of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/japan">Japan</a> in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chugoku-region">Chūgoku region</a> of western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/honshu">Honshu</a>, facing the Inland Sea, with its capital at Okayama. It was created after the abolition of the domains in 1871 and covers the old provinces of Bizen, Bitchū and Mimasaka. It is known for <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bizen-ware">Bizen ware</a>, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/koraku-en">Kōraku-en</a> garden and the historic merchant quarter of Kurashiki.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/okayama-prefecture.jpg" alt="Okayama Prefecture" width="320" height="212" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Takuma Kimura · CC BY-SA 2.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Christmas_tree_lighting_(6471182605).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
